## 🛠️ Part 1: The Ultimate Bash Automation Script
This script chains domain mirror extraction, Retire.js execution, and jq filtering into a single automated pipeline. It automatically isolates libraries vulnerable to high-impact flaws like Prototype Pollution or RCE, saving you hours of manual grep sorting.
Create a file named hunt_js.sh on your machine:

nano hunt_js.sh

Paste the following automated script:

#!/bin/bash
# Target Definitions
TARGETS=("https://1w.run" "https://1w.cash" "https://1win.com")
WORKSPACE="$HOME/hunting/1win_automation"
USER_AGENT="Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 16_5 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/16.5 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1"

echo "[*] Initializing Workspace: $WORKSPACE"
mkdir -p "$WORKSPACE/assets"
cd "$WORKSPACE"
# 1. Scrape JS assets from all mirrors simultaneouslyfor URL in "${TARGETS[@]}"; do
    echo "[+] Extracting JS layers from: $URL"
    wget --spider --recursive --level=3 --no-check-certificate --quiet \
         --accept js \
         --user-agent="$USER_AGENT" \
         "$URL" -P "$WORKSPACE/assets"done

echo "[*] Updating Retire.js signature matrix..."
retire --update

echo "[*] Running deep CLI scan on compiled bundles..."# Scan the workspace, output structured JSON, filter for high/critical risks
retire --path "$WORKSPACE/assets" --outputformat json --outputpath raw_results.json --severity high
# 2. Extract actionable data using jqif [ -f raw_results.json ]; then
    echo -e "\n[!] HIGH SEVERITY VULNERABILITIES DETECTED:"
    echo "--------------------------------------------------"
    jq '.data[] | {file: .file, library: .results[].component, version: .results[].version, vulnerability: .results[].vulnerabilities[].info}' raw_results.json 2>/dev/null
    echo "--------------------------------------------------"else
    echo "[-] No critical known signatures isolated by Retire.js."fi

Save and run it:

chmod +x hunt_js.sh
./hunt_js.sh

